      ],
      "rationale": "8.EE.A.3 asks how many times as large one quantity is as another, each written as a single digit times a power of 10. Each item gives two quantities from one context, such as a town and a country, so the sizes mean something. The student divides the first factors and subtracts the exponents.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Subtracting the two numbers instead of dividing them.",
       "Answering with the difference of the powers, such as 2, instead of 10²."
      ],
